2025-09-10 13:11:26,110 [WARNING] Skipped idx=560: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The p73 gene encodes two main isoforms in humans: TAp73 and DeltaNp73. TAp73 is the transcriptionally active form, while DeltaNp73 is a dominant-negative isoform. These isoforms are differentially expressed in various tissues, including the brain and glial tumors. In normal brain tissues, the expression of p73 is typically low or undetectable. However, in high-grade glial tumors, there is a strong up-regulation of TAp73, which may reflect the inactivation of the retinoblastoma pathway, leading to the activation of E2F transcription factors, as TAp73 is a known target of E2F1 gene. The study of TAp73 expression in brain tumors can provide insights into the retinoblastoma pathway-dependent tumor progression.'
